.\" man page create by R# package system.
.TH KOBAS 1 2000-1月 "kobas.plage" "kobas.plage"
.SH NAME
kobas.plage \- PLAGE pathway level analysis (KOBAS SNBEA)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIkobas.plage(\fBexpr\fR as any, 
\fBcls\fR as any, 
\fBgmt\fR as any, 
\fBmin_size\fR as integer = 5, 
\fBmax_size\fR as integer = 500, 
\fBfdr\fR as string = "BH", 
\fBdata_type\fR as string = "rseq", 
\fBnormalize\fR as boolean = TRUE, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
PLAGE pathway level analysis (KOBAS SNBEA)
 
 Score each gene set of the expression matrix with the PLAGE method (the first
 right singular vector of the row standardized gene set submatrix), then compare
 the activity scores between the two phenotype groups.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBexpr\fB \fR\- 
 the expression matrix (matrix object, \fBdataframe\fR or expression matrix file path).
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBcls\fB \fR\- the phenotype class labels, same as the \fBcls\fR parameter of \fBkobas.gsea\fR.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBgmt\fB \fR\- the gene set collection: a [Background](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.HTS.GSEA.Background) model or a GMT file path.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmin_size\fB \fR\- the minimum number of the mapped members of a gene set, default \fB5\fR.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmax_size\fB \fR\- the maximum number of the mapped members of a gene set, default \fB500\fR.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBfdr\fB \fR\- the multiple testing correction method, default \fBBH\fR.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBdata_type\fB \fR\- 
 the data type of the expression matrix: \fBrseq\fR (RNA-seq read counts, default) or
 \fBma\fR (microarray data).
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBnormalize\fB \fR\- 
 performs the data normalization before the analysis? Default \fBTRUE\fR: the RNA-seq
 data will be transformed by the log2 CPM with the prior count and the microarray
 data will be quantile normalized.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment.. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a \fBdataframe\fR with the gene set id as the row names and the columns: \fBname\fR,
 \fBdescription\fR, \fBsize\fR, \fBstatistic\fR, \fBpvalue\fR, \fBp_adjust\fR and \fBgenes\fR.
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
The differential analysis uses the classic Welch two sample t-test instead of the
 limma moderated t-test because there is no moderated t implementation in the
 GCModeller core library, so the p-values are slightly more conservative than the
 limma result.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
KOBAS
